{
  "arguments": {
    "query": "vLLM prefix caching block hash components"
  },
  "observation": {
    "evidence": [
      {
        "id": "E620d3ddaad5ad2054c752d19",
        "chunk_id": "779175155be2b4c482fd5c25",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "To improve privacy in shared environments, vLLM supports isolating prefix cache reuse through optional per-request salting.\nBy including a `cache_salt` in the request, this value is injected into the hash of the first block, ensuring that only requests with the same salt can reuse cached KV blocks.\nThis prevents timing-based attacks where an adversary could infer cached content by observing latency differences.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E8f67c161db19fd79595d505f",
        "chunk_id": "1b033b6229bf05e4e1b8f142",
        "parent_id": "e2f783bc52fc6d11dba52420",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L3-L13",
        "content": "Since prefix caching is almost a free lunch and won’t change model outputs, it has been widely used by many public endpoints (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, etc) and most open source LLM inference frameworks (e.g., SGLang).\nWhile there are many ways to implement prefix caching, vLLM chooses a hash-based approach.\nSpecifically, we hash each kv-cache block by the tokens in the block and the tokens in the prefix before the block:",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E881a6028445aaeece4403f8c",
        "chunk_id": "a756e1212e535b1d75e47a3f",
        "parent_id": "5e18fdc07bd0b1d756518f71",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L178-L192",
        "content": "In v0, when detecting block 3 is duplicated, we free block 3 and let Request 2 use block 1 instead, so its block table becomes `[0, 1]` in Time 1.\nHowever, the block table in vLLM v1 is append-only, meaning that changing the block table from `[0, 3]` to `[0, 1]` is not allowed.\nAs a result, we will have duplicated blocks for the hash key E-H.\nThis duplication will be eliminated when the request is freed.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E722fbbcc372bd4a54fbb26a3",
        "chunk_id": "ba41f1809d2ccb3fb1e3ecbb",
        "parent_id": "3094435fb062ce4a1b5f4dd4",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L47-L77",
        "content": "```text\nBlock 0\n    Parent hash: None\n    Token IDs: 1, 3, 7493, 1681, 1294, 1593, 3937, 9551, <p>, ..., <p>\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\nBlock 1\n    Parent hash: Block 0 hash\n    Token IDs: <p>, ..., <p>\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\nBlock 2\n    Parent hash: Block 1 hash\n    Token IDs: <p>, ..., <p>\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\nBlock 3\n    Parent hash: Block 2 hash\n    Token IDs: <p>, ..., <p>, 4\n    Extra hash: <image hash>\n```",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E68e142e762591a59b46c54fa",
        "chunk_id": "90ebebc245b50cfc4f3bdb91",
        "parent_id": "81dcd49c74edb12a4ee97db3",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L102-L117",
        "content": "The prefix caching in vLLM v1 is implemented in the KV cache manager.\nThe basic building block is the “Block” data class (simplified):",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E18df8d7de69a9bc239731abf",
        "chunk_id": "28bc81fe7e8f333b5d5c57d9",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "In the rest of this document, we first introduce the data structure used for prefix caching in vLLM v1, followed by the prefix caching workflow of major KV cache operators (e.g., allocate, append, free, eviction).\nFinally, we use an example to illustrate the end to end prefix caching workflow.\n**Cache Isolation for Security**",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E0362c6dc8d47bfd883c8dba8",
        "chunk_id": "410eaf3456d68525428df1d4",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "This offers protection without compromising performance.\n```json\n{\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant.\"},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Here is a document with details about the world series: ...\"},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Who won the world series in 2020?\"}\n  ],\n  \"cache_salt\": \"your-cache-salt\"\n}\n```",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E2e11ed500d592310a7422ca6",
        "chunk_id": "06a4698c9e4cb362ac120a20",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "With this setup, cache sharing is limited to users or requests that explicitly agree on a common salt, enabling cache reuse within a trust group while isolating others.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E1c5b7341c4d64d891d9a1cfe",
        "chunk_id": "7c1a6df7e7a23c7671ff1794",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "!!\n! note\nCache isolation is not supported in engine V0.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
